    underStress: "Under breach of the surrounding systems the vault holds: the attacker finds tokens. Under breach of the vault itself the structure has concentrated the loss, which is why its defences (separate identity, hardware keys, minimal detokenize) must be stronger than anything else in the estate. Under load the vault is on the critical path and must scale with the business.",
    adoption: "Pick the one value with the most systems touching it, usually the payment card number or a national identifier. Deploy or buy a vault with hardware backed keys and its own identity boundary. Move the point of entry to tokenize client side. Replace the value with the token in the primary database, then in logs and analytics, then in support tooling. Restrict detokenize to the named callers and turn on logging. Measure the reduction in systems holding the real value and in compliance scope.",
